jects if that's a rule\", async () => {});\n});\n```\n\n```python\n# engine/tests/integration/test_full_run.py\n\"\"\"End-to-end: synthetic connector → normalize → block/match → detect → resolve → db writes.\"\"\"\ndef test_full_pipeline_against_generated_dataset(tmp_path, pg_conn):\n    generate(seed=42, accounts=50, out_dir=tmp_path)\n    # execute_run equivalent, called directly (not via HTTP) against the seeded run\n    # assert conflicts/matches/resolutions counts are all > 0 and stats sum correctly\ndef test_full_pipeline_never_writes_to_sources_or_rulesets(tmp_path, pg_conn): ...\n```\n\n```python\n# engine/tests/eval/test_harness.py\nfrom eval.harness import run_harness  # once implemented\n\nclass TestHarness:\n    def test_baseline_exact_has_lower_f1_than_canon_full(self): ...\n    def test_escalation_precision_is_computed_against_manifest_ambiguous_entries(self): ...\n    def test_false_auto_apply_rate_is_zero_when_validate_node_active(self): ...\n    def test_ablation_without_validate_node_can_invent_values(self):\n        \"\"\"This ablation is REQUIRED by AGENTS.md — must demonstrate the risk validate() prevents.\"\"\"\n    def test_threshold_sweep_produces_monotonic_escalation_rate(self): ...\n```\n\n---\n\n### Priority order\n\n1. Install a test runner in `web/` and configure `pytest` in `engine/` — nothing else is runnable until then.\n2. `should_auto_apply` and `validate()` (once implemented) — these gate every auto-applied change; they're the highest-consequence functions in the repo.\n3. `requireReviewer`/`getReviewer` — auth is the only thing standing between the console and an org's full hierarchy.\n4. Zod ↔ Pydantic parity tests for `SurvivorshipRule`/`ruleSpecificity` — silent drift here breaks reproducibility, which AGENTS.md calls out explicitly.\n5. TDD skeletons for `normalize`/`detect`/`blocking`/`graph.resolve` — write them now so Phase 2/3 implementation lands against a spec, per AGENTS.md's \"ground truth first\" instruction.\n",
